      "side": 1,
      "message": "This bit really only applies to responses from UFPs and cables. For DisplayPort DFPs like Chromebook ports, this should be set to 0 in the ID header.\n\nFrom Section 6.4.4.3.1.1.5 of the PD Spec (Modal Operation Supported)\n\u003e The Modal Operation Supported bit is used to indicate whether or not the Product (either a Cable Plug or a device that can operate in the UFP role) is capable of supporting Modes. The Modal Operation Supported bit does not describe a DFP\u0027s Alternate Mode Controller functionality",
      "parentUuid": "2d3c0a4f_79b7b7ad",
